{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Flow.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Flow.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"flow flow","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Flow.md","fileName":"Flow.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Flow","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Player Experience Design]] [[Game Challenge Design]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Player Experience Design","Game Challenge Design","Autotelic Experience","Engagement","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf","agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Flow.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Flow.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"flow flow","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Flow.md","fileName":"Flow.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Flow","heading":"Flow","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Flow is a state of focused absorption in a challenging, uncertain activity. It is supported by understandable goals, clear feedback, concentrated attention, and a match between the participant's skill and the difficulty of the task.\n\nWhen challenge is too low, boredom threatens; when it is too high, anxiety or frustration takes over. Keeping the activity within this shifting channel can make it an [[Autotelic Experience]] and sustain [[Engagement]].\n\nFlow requires goals that can be acted on, feedback that supports adjustment, and demands that change as mastery grows. The ideal channel is only one possible shape of play: some games begin in frustration and let practice close the gap, while others pursue reflection or understanding rather than an uninterrupted flow state.\n\nThe same challenge-skill relationship can support creative work: excessive demand produces stress, insufficient demand produces boredom, and a demanding but attainable goal enables concentrated, productive absorption.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Player Experience Design","Game Challenge Design","Autotelic Experience","Engagement","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf","agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Flow.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Flow.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"flow flow","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Flow.md","fileName":"Flow.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Flow","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[advancedgamedesign.pdf]]\n[[agamedesignvocabulary.pdf]]\n[[agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Player Experience Design","Game Challenge Design","Autotelic Experience","Engagement","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf","agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}